Third-party attribution
=======================

Dispatcharr — https://github.com/Dispatcharr/Dispatcharr — AGPL-3.0-only
    The architecture of this project was informed by Dispatcharr's design: per-field channel
    overrides, hash-based stream identity, and its EPG matching approach (rapidfuzz ratio plus a
    regional bonus). No Dispatcharr source file has been copied into this repository yet.
    When a fragment is ported, the file carrying it gets a header naming the upstream path and
    commit, and this NOTICE is updated with the exact list.

iptv-org/database, iptv-org/iptv — Unlicense (public domain)
    Planned as seed data for channel identity, logos and country/language metadata.
    No data from these repositories is bundled in this repository.

iptv-org/epg — LICENSE file says Unlicense, package.json says "UNLICENSED"
    Not used as code. If an EPG grabber is ever integrated, it runs as an unmodified external
    process in its own container; its code is never vendored here.

